# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Repo-wide safety net.
#
# Each part of the stack (frontend / backend / app / cdn) also has its
# own .gitignore with rules specific to its build tool. This file only
# catches things that are generated anywhere in the tree, so a new
# folder is never accidentally committed with its build output.
#
# NOTE on env files: the real .env files are ignored, but the committed
# *templates* are explicitly allowed back in — they document which
# variables a deployment needs and are meant to be in the repo.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# Node dependencies
node_modules/

# Environment files — secrets. Templates are whitelisted below.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.template
!.env.sample

# Build / output directories
dist/
build/
out/
.next/
.medusa/
.cache/
.turbo/
.vite/
admin-static/

# Test / coverage output
coverage/
.nyc_output/

# Uploaded media — user content, never source
uploads/

# Logs
*.log
logs/
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*

# TypeScript incremental build info
*.tsbuildinfo

# Archives — these are big and are never source
*.zip
*.tar.gz
*.tgz
*.rar
*.7z

# Database dumps only — NOT hand-written .sql scripts. A blanket *.sql
# rule would hide operational scripts that are meant to be committed
# and run on the server (backend/admin-push-table.sql,
# backend/performance-indexes.sql), so match dump shapes instead.
*.dump
*.sql.gz
*-dump.sql
*_dump.sql
dump*.sql

# OS generated files
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
desktop.ini

# Editors / IDEs
.vscode/
.idea/
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?
